# 18. Integration Diagnostics

## 18.1 Philips TV

The provider may report:

- Last known reachability
- Authentication state
- Model and firmware where available
- Last successful command
- Last state refresh
- Current source and volume freshness
- Wake capability status
- API compatibility profile
- Recent command latency

Manual tests may include:

- Find TV again
- Test connection
- Test authentication
- Refresh capabilities
- Read current state
- Send non-destructive navigation test where appropriate

Model-specific behavior for `65PUS7800/12` must be verified before implementation.

## 18.2 Apple TV

The provider must clearly distinguish:

- Publicly supported capability
- HomeKit-derived capability
- Unavailable capability
- Experimental or unsupported implementation path

Diagnostics must not claim that a desired Apple TV feature is supported merely because it appears in the product specification.

## 18.3 HomeKit

The provider may report:

- Authorization state
- Home manager lifecycle state
- Number of homes and accessories
- Reachable accessory count
- Event-subscription health
- Last synchronization
- Capability-resolution failures

## 18.4 Hue Bridge

The provider may report:

- Bridge reachability
- Authentication state
- HTTPS connection health
- Event-stream state
- Last event time
- Resource synchronization state
- Command rate warnings
- Unreachable-light count
- Firmware version

Credentials and application keys must always be redacted.

