# 21. Automation Diagnostics

Automation diagnostics should include:

- Trigger received
- Trigger source
- Conditions evaluated
- Conditions that passed or failed
- Actions attempted
- Actions skipped
- Cooldown or deduplication decisions
- Loop-prevention decisions
- Execution duration
- Final result

Example user-facing explanation:

`Good Night did not run because the living-room TV was already off and the motion condition was still active.`

Advanced details may show the exact condition tree.

