# 34. Security Requirements

The Diagnostics System must:

- Treat plugin-provided metadata as untrusted input
- Enforce payload-size limits
- Redact before persistence where possible
- Redact again before export
- Protect local diagnostic files with platform data protection
- Avoid background uploads
- Use temporary files for export
- Delete temporary export files after sharing or cancellation
- Never permit logs to execute markup or code
- Escape user-controlled strings

---

# 35. Performance Metrics

Diagnostics may measure:

- Discovery latency
- Command dispatch latency
- Confirmed state latency
- Scene completion duration
- Automation execution duration
- Event-stream reconnect time
- HomeKit synchronization time
- Cache load time
- UI update delay
- Memory pressure events

Metrics must remain coarse enough to protect privacy.

---

# 36. Performance Budgets

Targets:

- Health summary from cached data: under 200 ms
- Provider snapshot aggregation: under 500 ms
- Standard reachability test: under 3 seconds
- Full multi-provider test: under 10 seconds
- Event append overhead: under 2 ms average
- Main-thread blocking caused by diagnostics: 0 operations over 16 ms
- Export generation for ordinary history: under 3 seconds
- Diagnostic store memory target: under 15 MB

