# 44. Failure Scenarios

## Scenario A: Diagnostics provider crashes or throws unexpectedly

Expected behavior:

- Isolate the provider failure
- Keep other providers available
- Record a sanitized platform issue
- Mark only the provider as unknown or unavailable

## Scenario B: Export fails

Expected behavior:

- Preserve local diagnostic history
- Delete incomplete temporary files
- Show a retry option
- Never upload automatically

## Scenario C: Recovery succeeds after the user leaves the screen

Expected behavior:

- Update health state silently
- Avoid unexpected navigation
- Show a subtle resolved status when the user returns

## Scenario D: Diagnostic test times out

Expected behavior:

- Cancel underlying work
- Mark result as timed out
- Offer a relevant next step
- Avoid indefinite progress

## Scenario E: Conflicting provider results

Expected behavior:

- Preserve both facts
- Lower confidence in root-cause inference
- Present a neutral explanation
- Avoid claiming certainty

