# 46. Acceptance Criteria

The Diagnostics System is ready for initial release when:

1. Aura can produce an overall health summary.
2. Each active integration exposes a provider snapshot.
3. Current issues are explained in user-friendly language.
4. One provider failure does not break the diagnostics screen.
5. Manual tests are cancellable and time-bounded.
6. Safe recovery actions can be executed from diagnostics.
7. Destructive recovery actions require confirmation.
8. Scene partial failures show per-action outcomes.
9. Automation failures show trigger, condition and action context.
10. Discovery sessions expose useful sanitized summaries.
11. Diagnostic history remains bounded.
12. Exports are user initiated.
13. Exports contain no credentials or secret values.
14. Privacy redaction is covered by automated tests.
15. Health updates do not block the main actor.
16. Accessibility requirements are met.
17. Real-hardware failure and recovery scenarios are validated.

